Expected elements: present

Every must-show is present; nothing forbidden appears. Typographically this is a strong dense surface: two mono sizes used deliberately (8.41px advance ≈14px in Code, 7.45px ≈12.5px in Call Trace and Values), numeric columns cleanly right-aligned (opcodes to x=1519, values to x=1407), and frame name vs path separated 15.52:1 / 5.47:1.

Round changes: (a) LANDED — current-line arm glyph at line 32 measures #67e8f9 on #334155 = 7.14:1 (claim 7.16); the non-current glyph on line 29 is 5.47:1. (b) UNVERIFIABLE HERE — "COST · MANA" occupies x1542-1611 of a 380px label column, so it has no reason to break at 1920; only a narrow capture can confirm it. (c) PARTLY — bar "128 / 1,315" matches Call Trace grouping, and the Values-pane exemption is correct (they are program Field values); but "88000 / 200000" at y=638 is the same N/M construct as the bar, is a resource count not a copyable datum, and is ungrouped. (d) The Code pane's bottom fade dims a complete line — line 61's dominant ink is 3.33:1 where the identical token on line 58 is 10.21:1.

I withdraw the "provenance row is too quiet" concern: its paragraph is the pane's largest and brightest prose (6.78px/char, 21.8px pitch, 6.75:1).

Top fixes: give section headings a level distinct from row labels; stop the fade before the last full code line.

Rating: 7/10

